  "problem": "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $x\\in {3,7}.$ \n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)\u21d4B(x)?$\n\n- $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N$ is equivalent to  $x\\in N.$\n- $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N$ if and only if $x\\in {3,7}.$\n- If $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N$ then $x\\in {3,7},$ or if $x\\in {3,7}$ then $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N.$",
